\f0\fs26 \cf0 We propose the following steps to extract and analyze the data for completeness. First, the appropriate expected data will be identified for each column, such as date written in month/date/year format, string, or integer.  Second, multiple CVS files or databases will be merged using a left union, with the \'93date\'94 being the connecting key. Then, the first 100 rows of the merged database will be extracted. From that 100 rows, multiple checks will be performed on the data, such as confirming all rows meet the expected data format, data in missing rows automatically converted to some approved data that identify the data is missing (i.e. \'930\'94 or \'93N/A\'94, as appropriate), and related actions.\
A testing function will be developed using the Python unittest framework to confirm all extracted rows meet the required data expectations. This will provide feedback to the researchers to adjust the program as needed.}